==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=head-on}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|head on}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} [[direct|Direct]], [[abrupt]], [[blunt]] or [[unequivocal]]; not [[prevaricating]].
#: ''a '''head-on''' approach to a problem''
# Of a collision, from the front or in the direction of motion.
#: ''Getting into a '''head-on''' collision is dangerous.''

====Usage notes====
* The adjective is also '''head on''', especially when appearing after the verb, as in
*: ''She likes to tackle problems '''head on'''.''

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|head-on collision}}

